& [CanonicalIdentity] is exact
  + [canonical_uuid] is d29478fa-1935-466c-ab78-4965864f8756
  + [profile] is cantor-process-procedure-experiment/0.1
  + [requirement_set] is CPPE-001 through CPPE-040
  + [upstream_SMTC_signature_uuid] is 810f24e8-3d1c-4074-ae57-706f8f63e892
  + [authority_grade] is future_separately_claimed_effectless_software_experiment
  + [canonical_source_specification] is this file

& [ProcedureIdentity] is content and purpose bound
  + ProcedureCandidate binds author, provenance, purpose, scope, language profile, source, digest, SOP anchors, schemas, process declarations, effects, bounds, and logical creation time
  + compiled identity binds normalized source, compiler, profile, IR, schemas, effect declaration, and bounds
  + revisions are immutable and inherit no admission, signature, catalogue, invocation, or capability
  + human names and aliases are versioned catalogue projections only

& [SOPAnchorContract] is exact
  + every anchor binds recognized signed artifact identity, version, digest, optional clause identity, intended use, and sensitivity
  + an invocation supplies only the pinned anchor set admitted for that procedure
  + stale, missing, invalidated, substituted, or scope-incompatible anchors fail closed
  - never: permit ambient search of the entire SOP fabric as implicit procedure input

& [TypeAndBoundSystem] is closed
  + values are null, boolean, bounded integer, bounded decimal, bounded text, bytes digest, identity reference, list, ordered map, record, tagged union, or typed fault
  + input, output, message, event, state, result, and fault schemas are explicit, versioned, normalized, and closed by default
  + collections, text, bytes, events, processes, messages, queues, maps, call depth, transitions, and traces have finite bounds
  + exact schema version is default and migration is separate

& [StateAndEffectSystem] is immutable and effectless
  + procedure and process state are versioned values replaced only by accepted transitions
  + allowed reads are typed invocation input and pinned admitted in-memory artefacts
  + allowed writes are returned values, messages, state successors, traces, receipts, and faults
  + no pointer, ambient object, global variable, hidden cache authority, or shared mutable state
  + no filesystem, network, database, system clock, randomness, process, provider, notification, Git, model call, unsafe code, or device effect

& [ProcessSemantics] are Simula-inspired and Cantor-native
  + one procedure declares one or more named process roles with local state, accepted and emitted messages, transitions, and terminal states
  + operations are bind, inspect, compare, branch, select, bounded map, emit, receive, yield, wait-logical, reactivate, join, return, and fault
  + detach, passivate, resume, and reactivate lower to explicit SerializedContinuation state
  + continuation binds procedure, process, program point, local state, inbox frontier, logical time, generation, budgets, and awaited condition
  + recursion, self-modification, runtime code loading, native stack capture, unrestricted inheritance, reflection, and unbounded event creation are prohibited

& [ProhibitedOperationSet] is closed for the first profile
  + recursion, unbounded iteration, unrestricted inheritance, dynamic allocation, pointer access, native stack capture, self-modification, runtime code loading, executable reflection, process creation beyond declared bounds, and undeclared storage are prohibited
  + system clock, randomness, environment, filesystem, network, database, subprocess, provider, notification, Git, model, unsafe code, device, and external-effect operations are prohibited
  + unknown or future operations are prohibited until a superseding processed profile admits them explicitly

& [SchedulerSemantics] are deterministic
  + at most one process transition operates in one scheduler step
  + other process states remain explicit and immutable
  + selection uses readiness, supplied logical time, causal predecessors, declared priority, and stable identity tie-break
  + every wait, loop, recurrence, and process walk has a static or invocation-bound termination measure
  + resource exhaustion returns a typed result without partial admission

& [PortableIR] is the semantic execution waist
  + Cantor Process IR version 0.1 contains types, schemas, constants, anchors, process definitions, control regions, state replacements, messages, logical scheduling, effects, bounds, faults, and source maps
  + normalization is independent of source formatting, model provider, host language, pointer layout, physical clock, register layout, and hardware vendor
  + all backends must preserve typed result and normalized semantic trace

& [SharedInferenceProtocol] is message based
  + every model, faculty, controller, user, and procedure participant is named with declared role
  + message binds session, sender, receiver, frame generation, SOP anchors, proposition kind, typed payload, evidence, logical time, causal predecessors, and expiry
  + kinds include propose, question, support, object, counter, qualify, withdraw, admit-candidate, refuse, yield, pass, and fault
  + NegotiatedFrame contains versioned propositions, conditions, constraints, evidence, objections, participants, and policy
  + Cantor validates and routes records but cannot promote agreement, majority, compilation, or speed to truth or authority

& [TokenRingStability] is one bounded negotiation experiment
  + one required participant holds the logical turn token at a time
  + pass means no generation-changing proposal, objection, qualification, or withdrawal
  + stable candidate requires every exact required participant to pass one complete cycle over the same frame and policy generation
  + any frame, participant, anchor, policy, proposal, objection, or qualification change resets incomplete pass state
  + silence, absence, timeout, tool failure, and stale pass are not assent
  + stable candidate remains subject to Observer admission

& [ProcedureLifecycle] separates authorities
  + lifecycle is proposed, parse-rejected, validated, compiled, verification-failed, verification-passed, admission-refused, admitted, suspended, revoked, or superseded
  + validation, compilation, verification, admission, catalogue insertion, invocation, and revocation each emit a distinct receipt from a named principal
  + no earlier phase implies a later phase

& [CompilerContract] is deterministic
  + canonical procedure forms lower to canonical Process IR with compiler identity, diagnostics, source map, effect table, bounds, and cost estimate
  + unknown construct, ambiguous type, prohibited operation, invalid anchor, or unsupported version fails closed
  + compilation neither verifies nor admits

& [VerifierContract] is independent from compilation disposition
  + checks type and schema closure, termination measure, resource bounds, effects, anchors, lifecycle, nondeterminism, prohibited operations, and normalized replay
  + verification receipt states evidence, residuals, and exact compiler and IR identity
  + compiler success cannot be its only verification evidence

& [AdmissionContract] is Observer owned
  + admission consumes exact source, compiler, IR, validation, verification, anchor, effect, bound, and policy identities
  + disposition names permitted invocation context and revocation conditions
  + admission applies to one exact compiled candidate only

& [ModelAuthorshipBoundary] is fail-closed
  + a model may emit a ProcedureCandidate through the same schema as a human or importer
  + it cannot self-sign, self-verify, self-admit, persist, broaden schema, grant capability, invoke itself, or access undeclared input
  + rejection may be returned for a later separately authored repair turn

& [CatalogueAndRevocation] preserve exact status
  + first catalogue is supplied immutable in-memory state
  + insertion requires exact active AdmissionDisposition
  + lookup returns exact identity, version, digest, admission, and revocation state
  + revocation and supersession prevent future invocation without deleting source, receipts, traces, or results

& [InvocationContract] closes one bounded execution
  + request pins caller, purpose, admitted procedure, schemas, input, anchors, policy, participants, logical time, steps, memory, and expected output
  + result contains typed output or fault, final procedure and process states, normalized trace, consumed budgets, residuals, and proof refs
  + stale procedure, schema, anchor, compiler, verifier, policy, catalogue, participant, frame, or invocation fails closed

& [FaultAndVersionContract] preserves safe refusal
  + faults name phase, category, subject identities, expected and observed versions, evidence, consumed budget, trace location, and safe residual
  + unsupported or stale source, schema, IR, compiler, verifier, policy, SOP anchor, catalogue, participant, frame, procedure, or invocation version fails before execution or successor admission
  + first-profile compatibility is exact and any migration is a separately identified deterministic transform with diagnostics, loss, and proof
  + faults never grant fallback capability or erase the rejected candidate and receipt lineage

& [ToolInferenceSeam] is explicit multi-pass coordination
  + model emits structured proposal or invocation request
  + controller stops generation at the tool boundary
  + Cantor runs externally and returns a structured result
  + result becomes explicit context for a later inference pass
  - never: claim direct hidden activation, K/V cache, weight, or uninterrupted-forward-pass sharing

& [TruthAndAuthorityBoundary] is permanent
  + deterministic means repeatable under exact inputs
  + stable means the required pass cycle completed
  + compiled means a canonical lowering exists
  + verified means declared static and replay obligations passed
  + admitted means Observer authorized the exact bounded procedure context
  + none alone proves truth, safety, fitness, consent, or external effect authority

& [AuthorityAndEffectBoundary] is the enforceable outer wall
  + ProcedureCandidate authorship, successful compilation, verification, admission, and invocation remain different authorities
  + first-profile procedures may produce only immutable in-memory state, messages, traces, receipts, typed output, or faults
  + live provider, clock, randomness, filesystem, network, database, process, notification, Git, unsafe code, device, and external effects are absent
  + any requirement for a prohibited effect invalidates this profile rather than silently widening it

& [FirstExperimentAndProof] may be separately claimed after phase-lock validation
  + CPPE-I01 through CPPE-I09 define machine-form-first future slices
  + hand-authored and model-shaped two-process candidates use the same pipeline
  + proof includes validation, deterministic compile, verification, fake admission, in-memory catalogue, interpreter, token-ring stability, replay, stale refusal, resource refusal, and fake controller transcript
  + no live model provider, textual syntax requirement, persistence, alternative backend, or external effect is released

